// Rule:        UAC bypass via ms-settings protocol handler hijack
// Tactics:     Privilege Escalation, Defense Evasion
// Techniques:  T1548.002 (Bypass User Account Control), T1112 (Modify Registry)
// Source:      Sysmon EventID 13 (registry value set), HarborlightDental_CL
// Seen in:     Q3.1 - reg.exe set ms-settings\shell\open\command to C:\Users\Public\taskhostw.exe (02:40-02:42 UTC)
// Severity:    High
// Tuning:      Legitimate software almost never writes this key under a user hive. Expect very few false positives.
HarborlightDental_CL
| where EventID == 13
| where TargetObject has @"_Classes\ms-settings\shell\open\command" or TargetObject has @"_Classes\ms-settings\shell\open\command\DelegateExecute"
| project EventTime, host, Image, TargetObject, Details
